ve a Roman domination number of 5 (satisfying the $5 > 3$ relationship)[2].\n*   **Definitions:**\n    *   **Roman Domination Number ($\\gamma_{Rom}(G)$):** The minimum weight of a Roman dominating function on a graph[6].\n    *   **Radius (rad(G)):** The minimum eccentricity among all vertices in the graph, representing the distance from the \"most central\" vertex to the farthest vertex[7][8].\n    *   **Total Domination Number ($\\gamma_t(G)$):** The minimum cardinality of a set of vertices such that every vertex in the graph is adjacent to at least one vertex in the set[9].\n\nThis work contributes to the broader field of domination in graphs, where researchers often seek to establish bounds and inequalities between different domination-related parameters and structural metrics like the radius and diameter[1][10].\n\nSources:\n[1] [ijsdr.org](https://vertex\n<truncated 637 bytes>\n[kemdiktisaintek.go.id](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFrHjXqfwPh_JCXPVjCKyjA-JGVqHn59UT4RVqZ4AJTXN6xp1tiNwvm6_jQyWp2JKw31LRoCYfq0kiBuY3FB_rCHumGSqUg5GMWnB8_wuqal3rlJPs5WAgnK-va8X6eORZ0KkytHf61R9jN4eky9w76n4mKjeNTdaWWoDAMOttPxRtkHdsnoOVYpJlvr9_VRQm0BaxizrqsgKs-nkm-xtfMcW05S60t_11s2FHWGCPLhXUjPIw97wWzetsKAk9eC2rTxZDlBsYVkyGjNalIoPLdow==)\n[5] [ijsdr.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH63LSluN2g6TQ-_OkHYMvMU8U2i4qmcyVxXTW6Xs0mJQSjGZfDf5Zj0MAyyu2UOpmEwpH6YfwCjHh2AVqeDvReDQjDnCnaP8k9sg8JxRn2cGFZfsht69sowZNgSju0t8FhB8k=)\n[6] [worldscientific.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHI1oWyDumCC4uIAE59OE9a1O5X5y9aMULp53ffDccM0Eba9Mnx8HPPxf71DICAEhkZNFO3rvwXtgg4vPsqMB9SnWkJ7T1KGDBVwQ5eFg9BrFz6_42YaxqDb_2hCyFHdbvmjx_guVMacUhQPWnx3s17Cv6064JvamtTVkzJYflKaGu-rBcCPA==)\n[7] [scribd.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEQzjsmSy0B1KFlX1VZPEzxA5DhaE885VUPKVcKpiqJYDbAq2TOaaZu0ctO549dEtZiANDGaeW0yaJ0ecC8TGbl9pwL4-CLkHHZFulABp1ilA22-7WE3Qr_VQ_oBHg-7JAwItWdhg