{"step_index":129,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:58:49Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T16:58:49+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T16:58:49+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/tools/audit_sample.py`\nTotal Lines: 276\nTotal Bytes: 13433\nShowing lines 70 to 110\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n70:     *trivial*  — the statement is already known, is implied by another\n71:                  survivor, or its hypothesis does no work.\n72:     *weak*     — it survives, but on too little evidence to mean much: a\n73:                  handful of graphs in its class, or a class the corpus barely\n74:                  represents.\n75:     *promising*— it survives on real evidence. Split by whether the class\n76:                  hypothesis is load-bearing, because a bound that holds for all\n77:                  graphs is a different kind of result from one that needs its\n78:                  class.\n79: \n80:     Only the *promising* rows need human thought; the rest carry a stated\n81:     reason that can be confirmed or overturned quickly.\n82:     \"\"\"\n83:     if record[\"known_as\"]:\n84:         return \"trivial:known\"\n85:     if record[\"subsumed_by\"]:\n86:         return \"trivial:subsumed\"\n87:     base_only = set(record[\"classes\"]) <= BASE_HYPOTHESES\n88:     if record[\"decorative\"] and not base_only:\n89:         return \"trivial:decorative\"\n90:     if record[\"support_generation\"] is not None and record[\"support_generation\"] < 20:\n91:         return \"weak:low-support\"\n92:     if record[\"decorative\"]:\n93:         return \"promising:universal\"\n94:     return \"promising:class\" if not base_only else \"promising:universal\"\n95: \n96: \n97: BUCKET_ORDER = (\"trivial:known\", \"trivial:subsumed\", \"trivial:decorative\",\n98:                 \"weak:low-support\", \"promising:universal\", \"promising:class\")\n99: \n100: \n101: def main() -> int:\n102:     ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n103:     ap.add_argument(\"--results\", default=os.path.join(\"results\", \"cegis_results.json\"))\n104:     ap.add_argument(\"--top\", type=int, default=100)\n105:     ap.add_argument(\"--json\", default=os.path.join(\"results\", \"audit_top.json\"))\n106:     ap.add_argument(\"--latex\", default=\"\")\n107:     ap.add_argument(\"--normalise\", action=\"store_true\",\n108:                     help=\"collapse restatements (same canonical body and \"\n109:                          \"hypothesis, different surface form). Off by default so \"\n110:                          \"the published listing and Table 2 stay reproducible.\")\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
