{"step_index":146,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:59:36Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-11T16:59:36+02:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-11T16:59:36+02:00\nFile Path: `file:///mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/lean_project/LeanProject/GraphInvariants.lean`\nTotal Lines: 222\nTotal Bytes: 11395\nShowing lines 1 to 100\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: /-\n2: GraphInvariants.lean — a small, faithful Lean 4 / mathlib formalization layer for\n3: the graph invariants that appear in the *simplest* CEGIS survivors, so that the\n4: machine-generated conjectures are well-formed `theorem … := sorry` goals the\n5: DeepSeek-Prover-V2 backend (and the kernel) can actually act on.\n6: \n7: Scope is deliberately small. Invariants already in mathlib are reused directly:\n8: \n9:   order n            → `Fintype.card V`        (aliased `SimpleGraph.order`)\n10:   size m             → `G.edgeFinset.card`     (aliased `SimpleGraph.size`)\n11:   minimum_degree δ   → `G.minDegree`           (mathlib)\n12:   maximum_degree Δ   → `G.maxDegree`           (mathlib)\n13:   clique_number ω    → `G.cliqueNum`           (mathlib)\n14:   independence_num α → `G.indepNum`            (mathlib)\n15:   chromatic_number χ → `G.chromaticNumber`     (mathlib, ℕ∞)\n16: \n17: Invariants *not* in mathlib but faithfully definable in a few lines are defined\n18: here (domination family). Harder invariants (zero forcing, residue, Roman\n19: domination, …) are intentionally out of scope: conjectures referencing them are\n20: filtered out of the prove set rather than formalized incorrectly.\n21: -/\n22: import Mathlib\n23: \n24: open scoped Classical\n25: \n26: namespace SimpleGraph\n27: \n28: variable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\n29: \n30: /-- Order of `G`: the number of vertices. -/\n31: def order (_G : SimpleGraph V) : ℕ := Fintype.card V\n32: \n33: /-- Size of `G`: the number of edges. -/\n34: noncomputabl\n<truncated 1953 bytes>\ner number `sl(G)`: the least `t` with `t + (sum of the t largest degrees) ≥ n`.\n70: A classical lower bound on the domination number. -/\n71: noncomputable def slaterNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n72:   sInf { t | (Fintype.card V) ≤ t + ((G.degreesDesc).take t).sum }\n73: \n74: /- ── Zero forcing family ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -/\n75: \n76: /-- One zero-forcing colour-change step: a blue vertex with a unique white\n77: neighbour forces it blue. -/\n78: noncomputable def forcingStep (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n79:     (S : Finset V) : Finset V :=\n80:   S ∪ Finset.univ.filter (fun w => w ∉ S ∧ ∃ v ∈ S, G.neighborFinset v \\ S = {w})\n81: \n82: /-- Zero-forcing closure: iterate the step `|V|` times (a fixpoint is reached, as\n83: each non-final step adds at least one vertex). -/\n84: noncomputable def forcingClosure (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n85:     (S : Finset V) : Finset V :=\n86:   (G.forcingStep)^[Fintype.card V] S\n87: \n88: /-- `S` is a zero-forcing set if its closure is everything. -/\n89: def IsZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n90:   G.forcingClosure S = Finset.univ\n91: \n92: /-- Zero forcing number `Z(G)`: minimum size of a zero-forcing set. -/\n93: noncomputable def zeroForcingNumber (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] : ℕ :=\n94:   sInf { k | ∃ S : Finset V, S.card = k ∧ G.IsZeroForcingSet S }\n95: \n96: /-- A total zero-forcing set: zero-forcing and inducing no isolated vertex. -/\n97: def IsTotalZeroForcingSet (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj] (S : Finset V) : Prop :=\n98:   G.IsZeroForcingSet S ∧ ∀ v ∈ S, ∃ w ∈ S, G.Adj v w\n99: \n100: /-- Total zero forcing number `Z_t(G)`. -/\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
