{"step_index":157,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T14:59:57Z","thinking":"**Understanding the challenge's structure**\n\nThe task involves a graph theory conjecture that needs to be settled within a specific Lean 4 file. The challenge requires either a proof or a refutation of the conjecture, which is (nontrivial) ⇒ (radius + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number, using a kernel-checked proof. This implies either proving or disproving the conjecture.\n\n\n```lean\nimport Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic\nimport Mathlib.Tactic\n\n/-!\n# Challenge e20263a9\n\nGiven a graph, prove that if the graph is nontrivial, then its radius + 1 is less than or equal to its Roman domination number.\n-/\n\ndef is_nontrivial (G : Type) [Graph G] : Prop :=\n  ∃ v w : G, v ≠ w\n\ndef radius (G : Type) [Graph G] : ℕ :=\n  sorry\n\ndef roman_domination_number (G : Type) [Graph G] : ℕ :=\n  sorry\n\ntheorem prove_e20263a9 (G : Type) [Graph G] :\n  is_nontrivial G → (radius G + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number G := by\n  sorry\n\ntheorem refute_e20263a9 (G : Type) [Graph G] :\n  ¬ (is_nontrivial G → (radius G + 1) ≤ roman_domination_number G) := by\n  sorry\n```\n\n**Reassessing proof direction**\n\nThe conjecture, relating graph radius and Roman domination number, needs verification. It's unclear whether a proof or refutation will be feasible. Initially, attempting a direct proof seems appropriate. However, the requirements allow refutation if a counterexample is found. It's crucial to explore potential counterexamples.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c \\\"\\nimport networkx as nx\\nfrom graphcalc.graphs.invariants.domination import roman_domination_number\\n\\ndef test_graph(G, name):\\n    if not nx.is_connected(G) or G.number_of_nodes() < 2:\\n        return\\n    rad = nx.radius(G)\\n    rom = roman_domination_number(G)\\n    if rad + 1 > rom:\\n        print(f'COUNTEREXAMPLE FOUND! {name}: nodes={G.number_of_nodes()}, rad={rad}, rom={rom}, edges={list(G.edges())}')\\n        exit(0)\\n\\n# Test various generators\\nfor n in range(2, 20):\\n    test_graph(nx.path_graph(n), f'path_{n}')\\n    test_graph(nx.cycle_graph(n), f'cycle_{n}')\\n    test_graph(nx.wheel_graph(n), f'wheel_{n}')\\n    test_graph(nx.star_graph(n), f'star_{n}')\\n\\nfor n in range(3, 10):\\n    for k in range(1, n//2 + 1):\\n        try:\\n            test_graph(nx.circulant_graph(n, [1, k]), f'circulant_{n}_{k}')\\n        except: pass\\n\\nfor n in [3, 4, 5, 6, 7]:\\n    for k in range(1, n):\\n        if 2*k != n:\\n            test_graph(nx.generalized_petersen_graph(n, k), f'gpetersen_{n}_{k}')\\n\\nfor d in range(1, 5):\\n    test_graph(nx.hypercube_graph(d), f'hypercube_{d}')\\n\\nprint('All standard graph families passed!')\\n\\\"\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Test standard graph families\"","toolSummary":"\"Test standard networkx graph families\""}}]}
